 "standard_code": "JSS 1: Algebraic Processes",
 "standard_url": "https://nerdc.gov.ng/",
 "standard_text": "Use letters for numbers; write word problems in symbolic terms; simplify expressions by collecting like terms; substitute values. (summary of the NERDC JSS 1 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 1 maths worksheets on algebra: writing expressions from words, notation, collecting like terms, multiplying terms, expanding brackets and substitution. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "3a means 3 × a",
 "key_sub": "Only like terms can be added.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>In algebra a letter stands for an unknown number. 5n means 5 × n; n² means n × n.</li><li>Like terms have the same letters: 3x + 5x = 8x, but 3x + 5y stays as it is.</li><li>To substitute, replace each letter with its value and use BODMAS.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Simplify 4a + 3b − a + 2b</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>4a − a = 3a, 3b + 2b = 5b</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 3a + 5b</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>If x = 3, find 2x² − 1</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>2 × 9 − 1</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 17</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Adding unlike terms</td><td>2a + 3b cannot be simplified.</td></tr><tr><td>Writing 2x² as (2x)²</td><td>2x² = 2 × x².</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting the sign in front of a term</td><td>The sign belongs to the term after it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is a coefficient?",
   "a": "The number in front of a letter, like 7 in 7y."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is an expression?",
   "a": "Terms joined by + or −, with no equals sign."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is ab the same as ba?",
   "a": "Yes."
  }
 ],
